1
00:00:11,296 --> 00:00:16,864
Here’s The Emperor’s New Clothes by Hans Christian Andersen.

2
00:00:20,288 --> 00:00:25,184
Once upon a time, an emperor liked clothes very much.

3
00:00:25,792 --> 00:00:28,528
He wanted to buy some new clothes.

4
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:32,256
Two brothers came and lied to him,

5
00:00:32,656 --> 00:00:35,216
“We can make wonderful clothes!

6
00:00:35,584 --> 00:00:38,208
But only clever people can see them!”

7
00:00:39,024 --> 00:00:41,008
They pretended to make the clothes.

8
00:00:42,160 --> 00:00:45,488
The emperor’s officials couldn’t see the clothes,

9
00:00:46,144 --> 00:00:49,376
but they said, “What lovely clothes!”

10
00:00:50,176 --> 00:00:53,232
The emperor couldn’t see anything either,

11
00:00:53,568 --> 00:00:56,960
but he said, “They’re beautiful!”

12
00:00:57,808 --> 00:01:00,080
No one wanted to look silly.

13
00:01:01,264 --> 00:01:05,360
The emperor decided to show everyone his new clothes.

14
00:01:06,128 --> 00:01:08,592
People in the street praised them.

15
00:01:09,104 --> 00:01:11,520
They were afraid to look silly too!

16
00:01:12,496 --> 00:01:14,848
Suddenly, a boy shouted,

17
00:01:15,216 --> 00:01:18,800
“Look! The emperor has no clothes on!”

18
00:01:19,328 --> 00:01:21,120
Everyone looked at one another.

19
00:01:21,504 --> 00:01:23,008
They started laughing.

20
00:01:23,696 --> 00:01:27,648
The end! Did you like the story?

21
00:01:28,112 --> 00:01:29,872
Please tell me what you think!

